      "note": "Paper Table 3: Evaluation of three code-agent frameworks using different models. Accuracy = (N_Yes + 0.5 * N_Partial) / N_Total. Appearance score ranges 1-5 (GPT-4o graded). yes_rate/partial_rate/no_rate/start_failed are the raw test-case outcome distributions. 16 framework x model combinations across Bolt.diy, OpenHands, and Aider. WebGen-LM models are Qwen2.5-Coder-Instruct fine-tuned on Bolt.diy trajectories (7B/14B/32B sizes). WebGen-LM-32B achieves the highest accuracy (38.2%), surpassing the best proprietary model DeepSeek-R1 (27.8%). Claude-3.5-Sonnet on Bolt.diy has the highest appearance score (3.0) among general-purpose models."
