  "notes": "Benchmark for LLM agents generating multi-file websites from scratch. 101 instructions with 647 test cases across 3 major categories (Content Presentation, User Interaction, Data Management) and 13 minor categories.\n\nKey characteristics:\n- Agents must generate complete, functional websites (HTML/CSS/JS) from natural language instructions\n- Three frameworks evaluated: Bolt.diy (web-app generation), OpenHands (general code agent), Aider (terminal-based)\n- Evaluation via WebVoyager UI agent (Qwen2.5-VL-32B) that interacts with deployed sites\n- Appearance scored by GPT-4o on a 1-5 scale\n- Accuracy formula: (N_Yes + 0.5 * N_Partial) / N_Total\n- WebGen-LM: fine-tuned Qwen2.5-Coder-Instruct (7B/14B/32B) on 600 Bolt.diy trajectories via rejection sampling\n- UI agent testing aligns with manual testing 86-94% of the time (Table 5)\n\nFollow-up paper (arXiv:2509.22644) introduces WebGen-Agent, an improved scaffold that boosts Claude-3.5-Sonnet from 26.4% to 51.9%.\n\nFrom MMLab, The Chinese University of Hong Kong."
}
